          "quote": "Fusion welding also destroys the interlocked, elongated grain structure in the ODS material and replaces it with a much weaker cast structure. The as-solidified grains are generally either equiaxed or oriented parallel to the direction of heat flow. Accordingly, fusion welding often results in grain boundaries that lie transverse to the direction of maximum applied loads. Such boundaries seriously degrade the high-temperature performance of the joint.",
